Features of System Calls
Interface: Provides an interface between user programs and the operating system.

Protection: Allows privileged operations while protecting the system.

Kernel Mode: Temporarily switches the program from user mode to kernel mode.

Context Switching: Saves the current process state and switches to kernel mode.

Error Handling: Returns error codes when an operation fails.

Synchronization: Helps safely access shared resources.

How a System Call Works
A program requires a special OS resource.

The program makes a system call request.

The operating system identifies the request.

Control is transferred to the kernel.

The kernel performs the requested operation.

Control is returned to the program.

